invariant: INV-17
file: src/sha3_inverted_lanes.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha3-stack
reason: keccak_rounds_inverted counts its rounds again, so the count and
  the table's address take two registers. Built with the frame pointer,
  as macOS builds it, clang then writes theta's value d2 to a slot below
  the stack pointer. The value stays there after the call. The part
  builds bin/sha3_equiv_test_host for x86-64 with -fno-omit-frame-pointer
  under clang, and its search of the stack finds d2. On an Apple silicon
  Mac, make check's check-rosetta finds it too.

--- old
    for (const uint64_t *rc = RC;; rc += 2) {
        keccak_round_inverted(scratch, a, rc[0]);
        keccak_round_inverted(a, scratch, rc[1]);
        const uint64_t *last = RC + 22;
        KECCAK_ASM_OUTPUT(last);
        if (rc == last) {
            break;
        }
    }
--- new
    for (int round = 0; round < 24; round += 2) {
        keccak_round_inverted(scratch, a, RC[round]);
        keccak_round_inverted(a, scratch, RC[round + 1]);
    }
